1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:03,700
This donor kebab shop in New York City needs to be on your devour list.

2
00:00:04,059 --> 00:00:08,980
Donor House in the East Village starts by spraying their bread with water and pressing it down to look like this.

3
00:00:09,480 --> 00:00:13,660
They slice this bread into fours to make their bread pockets for each kebab.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,079
Look at how fresh these look.

5
00:00:17,460 --> 00:00:24,940
Each donor kebab gets their creamy white garlic sauce, their chunky roasted pepper sauce, lettuce, cabbage, tomatoes,

6
00:00:25,280 --> 00:00:25,820
and red onions.

7
00:00:25,940 --> 00:00:31,019
We couldn't say no to their insanely juicy beef donor, which they pack in there.

8
00:00:31,280 --> 00:00:38,359
They close this beast up, wrap it, and place it in a box with a weirdly familiar logo.

9
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:43,460
I'm always amazed at how absolutely packed their donor kebabs are.

10
00:00:43,719 --> 00:00:47,560
They're meaty, crunchy, saucy, and just downright devour worthy.

